<title>UK: Cellnet chief quits - press reports.</title>
<headline>Cellnet chief quits - press reports.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Howard Ford has quit as managing director of mobile phone group Cellnet, owned by British Telecommunications Plc and Securicor Plc, after 30 months in charge, according to press reports.</p>
<p>No reason for the reported departure was given, though the Financial Times said Ford was expected to take up a position at a rival to British Telecom.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
